#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 1. Install the required packages {#step-1-install-the-required-packages}"
msgstr "Hakbang 1. I-install ang mga kinakailangang package {#step-1-install-the-required-packages}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Executor and the directed execution model require the `samplomatic` package:\n"
msgstr "Kailangan ng Executor at ng directed execution model ang `samplomatic` package:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Version notes\">\n"
"- `qiskit-ibm-runtime` v0.48.0 is recommended because it adds the `meas_level = \"both\"` option and the `local_c1` twirling group.\n"
"- `qiskit >= 2.3.0` is required.\n"
"- `samplomatic >= 0.18.0` is required.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Mga Tala sa Bersyon\">\n"
"- Inirerekomenda ang `qiskit-ibm-runtime` v0.48.0 dahil idinadagdag nito ang opsyon na `meas_level = \"both\"` at ang twirling group na `local_c1`.\n"
"- Kinakailangan ang `qiskit >= 2.3.0`.\n"
"- Kinakailangan ang `samplomatic >= 0.18.0`.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"imports\"></span>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 2. Change the imports {#step-2-change-the-imports}"
msgstr "Hakbang 2. Baguhin ang mga import {#step-2-change-the-imports}"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Sampler:**\n"
msgstr "**Sampler:**\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Executor:**\n"
msgstr "**Executor:**\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"circuit-samplex\"></span>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 3. Replace PUB tuples with a `QuantumProgram` {#step-3-replace-pub-tuples-with-a-quantumprogram}"
msgstr "Hakbang 3. Palitan ang mga PUB tuple ng `QuantumProgram` {#step-3-replace-pub-tuples-with-a-quantumprogram}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Instead of passing a list of tuples (PUBs), when using Executor, you build a `QuantumProgram` and append _items_ to it.\n"
msgstr "Sa halip na magpasa ng listahan ng mga tuple (PUBs), kapag gumagamit ng Executor, bumubuo ka ng `QuantumProgram` at nagdaragdag ng _mga item_ dito.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A `QuantumProgram` accepts _circuit_ items and _samplex_ items:\n"
msgstr "Tumatanggap ang `QuantumProgram` ng mga item na _circuit_ at mga item na _samplex_:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`append_circuit_item`: Appends a `CircuitItem`, which is a circuit and (optionally) its\n"
"parameter values. It is executed as-is, without any randomization. \n"
msgstr ""
"`append_circuit_item`: Nagdaragdag ng `CircuitItem`, na isang circuit at (opsyonal) ang mga\n"
"parameter value nito. Isinasagawa ito nang as-is, nang walang anumang randomization. \n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  Use this when you just want to sample a circuit, exactly as Sampler would with a PUB that has no\n"
"  twirling; for example, when submitting a plain sampling job, or when you already manually included any\n"
"  variants you want.\n"
"- `append_samplex_item`: Appends a `samplexItem`, which is a *template circuit* plus a\n"
"  *samplex* that generates randomized parameter sets on the server side. \n"
msgstr ""
"  Gamitin ito kapag gusto mo lamang mag-sample ng circuit, katulad ng ginagawa ng Sampler sa isang PUB na walang\n"
"  twirling; halimbawa, kapag nagsusumite ng plain sampling job, o kapag manu-mano mo nang isinama ang anumang\n"
"  mga variant na gusto mo.\n"
"- `append_samplex_item`: Nagdaragdag ng `samplexItem`, na isang *template circuit* kasama ang isang\n"
"  *samplex* na bumubuo ng randomized na mga parameter set sa server side. \n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  Use this\n"
"  when you want the circuit's content randomized. The primary case is with \n"
"  twirling (gate or measurement) or noise injection. This capability replaces\n"
"  Sampler's built-in twirling.\n"
msgstr ""
"  Gamitin ito\n"
"  kapag gusto mong i-randomize ang content ng circuit. Ang pangunahing kaso ay sa \n"
"  twirling (gate o measurement) o noise injection. Pinapalitan ng kakayahang ito\n"
"  ang built-in twirling ng Sampler.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A single `QuantumProgram` can accept both item types; each appended item is executed as an\n"
"independent task and produces its own entry in the results. In general, use `append_circuit_item` when your circuit does not need to be randomized. Otherwise, use `append_samplex_item`.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang isang `QuantumProgram` ay maaaring tumanggap ng parehong uri ng item; bawat idinagdag na item ay isinasagawa bilang\n"
"independent na task at gumagawa ng sarili nitong entry sa mga resulta. Sa pangkalahatan, gamitin ang `append_circuit_item` kapag hindi kailangang i-randomize ang iyong circuit. Kung hindi, gamitin ang `append_samplex_item`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The next sections show each in turn: parameterized circuits that use \n"
"`append_circuit_item`, and migrating twirling by using `append_samplex_item`.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ipinapakita ng mga susunod na seksyon ang bawat isa nang paisa-isa: mga parameterized circuit na gumagamit ng \n"
"`append_circuit_item`, at ang paglipat ng twirling gamit ang `append_samplex_item`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In the following code examples, `isa_circuit` refers to the circuit that has been transpiled to conform to the target backend's [Instruction Set Architecture](/guides/transpile#instruction-set-architecture) (ISA). This `isa_circuit` contains two parameters.\n"
msgstr "Sa mga sumusunod na halimbawa ng code, ang `isa_circuit` ay tumutukoy sa circuit na na-transpile upang sumunod sa [Instruction Set Architecture](/guides/transpile#instruction-set-architecture) (ISA) ng target backend. Ang `isa_circuit` na ito ay naglalaman ng dalawang parameter.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"param-circuits\"></span>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 3a. Migrate parameterized circuits {#step-3a-migrate-parameterized-circuits}"
msgstr "Hakbang 3a. Ilipat ang mga parameterized circuit {#step-3a-migrate-parameterized-circuits}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"With Sampler, parameter values are the second element of the PUB tuple. With Executor,\n"
"pass them as `circuit_arguments` to `append_circuit_item`.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa Sampler, ang mga parameter value ay ang ikalawang elemento ng PUB tuple. Sa Executor,\n"
"ipasa ang mga ito bilang `circuit_arguments` sa `append_circuit_item`.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Executor**\n"
msgstr "**Executor**\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"twirling\"></span>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 3b. Migrate built-in twirling to explicit annotations {#step-3b-migrate-built-in-twirling-to-explicit-annotations}"
msgstr "Hakbang 3b. Ilipat ang built-in twirling patungo sa explicit na mga annotation {#step-3b-migrate-built-in-twirling-to-explicit-annotations}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This is the most significant change. Sampler applies twirling for you by using options. With \n"
"Executor, you declare that intent explicitly by using annotated boxes and\n"
"a samplex (from [Samplomatic](/guides/directed-execution-model#samplomatic)).\n"
msgstr ""
"Ito ang pinakamahalagang pagbabago. Inilalapat ng Sampler ang twirling para sa iyo sa pamamagitan ng paggamit ng mga opsyon. Sa \n"
"Executor, idineklara mo ang intensyong iyon nang explicit sa pamamagitan ng paggamit ng mga annotated box at\n"
"isang samplex (mula sa [Samplomatic](/guides/directed-execution-model#samplomatic)).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Sampler (twirling by using options):**\n"
msgstr "**Sampler (twirling gamit ang mga opsyon):**\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Executor (twirling by using boxes and a samplex):**\n"
msgstr "**Executor (twirling gamit ang mga box at isang samplex):**\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Because the template circuit and samplex are built on the client side, you can\n"
"inspect and sample them locally to verify the output before sending anything to\n"
"hardware.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dahil ang template circuit at samplex ay binubuo sa client side, maaari mong\n"
"suriin at i-sample ang mga ito nang lokal upang i-verify ang output bago magpadala ng anuman sa\n"
"hardware.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"sample-local\"></span>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Verification: Sample the template circuit locally {#verification-sample-the-template-circuit-locally}"
msgstr "Pag-verify: I-sample ang template circuit nang lokal {#verification-sample-the-template-circuit-locally}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You can draw randomizations from the samplex and bind them to the template\n"
"circuit to confirm that the samplex is producing the parameter values you expect.\n"
"The parameter values returned by `samplex.sample` are directly compatible with the\n"
"template circuit's parameters.\n"
msgstr ""
"Maaari kang kumuha ng mga randomization mula sa samplex at i-bind ang mga ito sa template\n"
"circuit upang kumpirmahin na gumagawa ang samplex ng mga parameter value na inaasahan mo.\n"
"Ang mga parameter value na ibinabalik ng `samplex.sample` ay direktang compatible sa mga\n"
"parameter ng template circuit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To go further, you can verify that each randomization is logically equivalent to the\n"
"original circuit by, for example, converting both to `Operator` objects and comparing their unitary implementations (after\n"
"accounting for the `outputs[\"measurement_flips.<register>\"]` corrections that undo\n"
"measurement twirling), or by comparing expectation values from a local\n"
"`StatevectorSampler` or `StatevectorEstimator` run. See the Samplomatic\n"
"[Samplex inputs and outputs](https://qiskit.github.io/samplomatic/guides/samplex_io.html)\n"
"guide for a complete walkthrough.\n"
msgstr ""
"Para umusad pa, maaari mong i-verify na ang bawat randomization ay logically equivalent sa\n"
"orihinal na circuit sa pamamagitan ng, halimbawa, pagko-convert ng pareho sa mga `Operator` object at paghahambing ng kanilang unitary implementation (pagkatapos\n"
"isaalang-alang ang mga `outputs[\"measurement_flips.<register>\"]` na pagwawasto na bumabawi sa\n"
"measurement twirling), o sa pamamagitan ng paghahambing ng mga expectation value mula sa isang lokal na\n"
"pagpapatakbo ng `StatevectorSampler` o `StatevectorEstimator`. Tingnan ang Samplomatic\n"
"[Samplex inputs and outputs](https://qiskit.github.io/samplomatic/guides/samplex_io.html)\n"
"guide para sa kumpletong walkthrough.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"shots\"></span>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 4. Change how shots are requested {#step-4-change-how-shots-are-requested}"
msgstr "Hakbang 4. Baguhin kung paano hinihiling ang mga shot {#step-4-change-how-shots-are-requested}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Move shots from the PUB to `QuantumProgram(shots=...)`.  In Executor, `shots` applies to the whole job. Submit multiple jobs if you need different shot counts.\n"
msgstr "Ilipat ang shots mula sa PUB patungo sa `QuantumProgram(shots=...)`.  Sa Executor, ang `shots` ay nalalapat sa buong job. Magsumite ng maraming job kung kailangan mo ng magkakaibang bilang ng shot.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"options\"></span>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 5. Update options as necessary {#step-5-update-options-as-necessary}"
msgstr "Hakbang 5. I-update ang mga opsyon kung kinakailangan {#step-5-update-options-as-necessary}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"There are fewer options available to Executor than Sampler, because\n"
"error-mitigation choices now live in your annotations and samplex instead of options.\n"
msgstr ""
"Mas kaunti ang mga opsyong available sa Executor kaysa sa Sampler, dahil\n"
"ang mga pagpipilian sa error-mitigation ay nasa iyong mga annotation at samplex na ngayon sa halip na sa mga opsyon.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "There is also a structural difference in where settings live. \n"
msgstr "May pagkakaiba rin sa istruktura kung saan naninirahan ang mga setting. \n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"- With Sampler,\n"
"everything, including choices that affect result post-processing, is configured on\n"
"the primitive's options or in the PUB. \n"
msgstr ""
"- Sa Sampler,\n"
"lahat, kabilang ang mga pagpipiliang nakakaapekto sa post-processing ng resulta, ay naka-configure sa\n"
"mga opsyon ng primitive o sa PUB. \n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"- With Executor, choices that affect how the job\n"
"results are shaped and post-processed are set on the [`QuantumProgram`](/guides/executor-input-output#inputs-quantum-programs), not on\n"
"`ExecutorOptions`. \n"
msgstr ""
"- Sa Executor, ang mga pagpipiliang nakakaapekto kung paano hinuhugis at pino-post-process ang mga resulta ng job\n"
"ay itinatakda sa [`QuantumProgram`](/guides/executor-input-output#inputs-quantum-programs), hindi sa\n"
"`ExecutorOptions`. \n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Examples:\n"
msgstr "Examples:\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Sampler      | Executor                    |\n"
"|--------------|-----------------------------|\n"
"| `shots`      | `QuantumProgram(shots=...)` |\n"
"| `meas_type` | `QuantumProgram(meas_level=...)` |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Sampler      | Executor                    |\n"
"|--------------|-----------------------------|\n"
"| `shots`      | `QuantumProgram(shots=...)` |\n"
"| `meas_type` | `QuantumProgram(meas_level=...)` |\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[`ExecutorOptions`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-models-executor-options) holds only lower-level execution and environment\n"
"settings that don't change the structure of the returned data. It has three top-level groups:\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang [`ExecutorOptions`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-models-executor-options) ay naghahawak lamang ng mas mababang-antas na execution at environment\n"
"settings na hindi nagbabago sa istruktura ng ibinalik na data. May tatlong top-level na grupo ito:\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`environment` ([`EnvironmentOptions`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-models-environment-options))\n"
msgstr "`environment` ([`EnvironmentOptions`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-models-environment-options))\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`execution` ([`ExecutionOptions`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-models-execution-options)): Contains fewer options than with Sampler.  For example, there  is no `meas_type` Executor option. \n"
msgstr "`execution` ([`ExecutionOptions`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-models-execution-options)): Naglalaman ng mas kaunting opsyon kaysa sa Sampler.  Halimbawa, walang `meas_type` na opsyon ang Executor. \n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "[`experimental`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-models-executor-options#experimental)\n"
msgstr "[`experimental`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-models-executor-options#experimental)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Notably, the `twirling` and `dynamical_decoupling` options exist in Sampler but not Executor. Instead, those option values are expressed through the directed execution model.\n"
msgstr "Kapansin-pansin, ang mga opsyong `twirling` at `dynamical_decoupling` ay umiiral sa Sampler ngunit hindi sa Executor. Sa halip, ipinapahayag ang mga halaga ng opsyong iyon sa pamamagitan ng directed execution model.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Example:**\n"
msgstr "**Example:**\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"run-job\"></span>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 6. Update the `run` command {#step-6-update-the-run-command}"
msgstr "Hakbang 6. I-update ang `run` command {#step-6-update-the-run-command}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The input to an Executor job is the program, instead of PUBs.\n"
msgstr "Ang input sa isang Executor job ay ang program, imbes na mga PUB.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"results\"></span>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 7. Change how you access results {#step-7-change-how-you-access-results}"
msgstr "Step 7. Baguhin kung paano mo ina-access ang mga resulta {#step-7-change-how-you-access-results}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In Executor, results are NumPy arrays, not `BitArray` objects.  Use the name string as the index (`result[0][\"meas\"]`) and get an `np.ndarray` back. There is no need to remember the `.data.<register>` attribute path.\n"
msgstr "Sa Executor, ang mga resulta ay mga NumPy arrays, hindi `BitArray` objects.  Gamitin ang name string bilang index (`result[0][\"meas\"]`) at makakakuha ka ng `np.ndarray` pabalik. Hindi na kailangang tandaan ang `.data.<register>` attribute path.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To update from Sampler to Executor, change `result[i].data.<reg> (BitArray)` to `result[i][\"<reg>\"] (np.ndarray)`, then rewrite `get_counts`-based post-processing as NumPy operations.\n"
msgstr "Para mag-update mula sa Sampler patungo sa Executor, palitan ang `result[i].data.<reg> (BitArray)` ng `result[i][\"<reg>\"] (np.ndarray)`, pagkatapos ay isulat muli ang `get_counts`-based post-processing bilang mga NumPy operations.\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Task                          | Sampler                                          | Executor                                    |\n"
"| ----------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| Get register data             | `result[0].data.meas`                            | `result[0][\"meas\"]`                         |\n"
"| Data type                     | `BitArray`                                        | `np.ndarray`                                |\n"
"| Counts dictionary             | `result[0].data.meas.get_counts()`              | Post-process the array manually             |\n"
"| Multiple registers            | `result[0].data.<name>` per register             | `result[0][\"<name>\"]` per register          |\n"
"| CircuitItem array shape       | -                                               | `(parameter_sets, shots, register_bits)`    |\n"
"| SamplexItem array shape       | -                                               | `(randomizations, parameter_sets, shots, register_bits)` |\n"
"| Undo measurement twirling     | Automatic                                        | `result[i][\"measurement_flips.<name>\"]` + XOR |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Task                          | Sampler                                          | Executor                                    |\n"
"| ----------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| Get register data             | `result[0].data.meas`                            | `result[0][\"meas\"]`                         |\n"
"| Data type                     | `BitArray`                                        | `np.ndarray`                                |\n"
"| Counts dictionary             | `result[0].data.meas.get_counts()`              | Post-process the array manually             |\n"
"| Multiple registers            | `result[0].data.<name>` per register             | `result[0][\"<name>\"]` per register          |\n"
"| CircuitItem array shape       | -                                               | `(parameter_sets, shots, register_bits)`    |\n"
"| SamplexItem array shape       | -                                               | `(randomizations, parameter_sets, shots, register_bits)` |\n"
"| Undo measurement twirling     | Automatic                                        | `result[i][\"measurement_flips.<name>\"]` + XOR |\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"Sampler's `BitArray` offers helpers (`get_counts`, `slice_bits`, `slice_shots`, `expectation_values`, and post-selection masks). Executor returns raw NumPy arrays so you can perform this post-processing with standard NumPy operations.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"twirled-results\"></span>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 8. Handle twirled results (bit-flip corrections) {#step-8-handle-twirled-results-bit-flip-corrections}"
msgstr "Step 8. Pangasiwaan ang mga twirled na resulta (bit-flip corrections) {#step-8-handle-twirled-results-bit-flip-corrections}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"When you apply measurement twirling through a `SamplexItem`, Executor returns the raw\n"
"(twirled) measurements plus the bit-flip corrections needed to undo the twirling.\n"
"You need to apply them manually; nothing is corrected implicitly. \n"
msgstr ""
"Kapag nag-apply ka ng measurement twirling sa pamamagitan ng `SamplexItem`, ibinabalik ng Executor ang raw\n"
"(twirled) na mga measurement kasama ang mga bit-flip correction na kailangan para i-undo ang twirling.\n"
"Kailangan mong i-apply ang mga ito nang manu-mano; walang anumang itinutuwid nang implicit. \n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "When using Executor, undo twirling explicitly by using the `measurement_flips.<reg>` corrections and an XOR, as shown in the following example:\n"
msgstr "Kapag gumagamit ng Executor, i-undo nang explicit ang twirling gamit ang mga `measurement_flips.<reg>` correction at isang XOR, gaya ng ipinapakita sa sumusunod na halimbawa:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "There is no equivalent step in Sampler because it undoes twirling for you.\n"
msgstr "Walang katumbas na hakbang sa Sampler dahil ito mismo ang nag-a-undo ng twirling para sa iyo.\n"

